SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine Financial Institutions Superintendent w
 arns consumers of potential financial scams during the holiday season
DESCRIPTION:Maine Financial Institutions Superintendent warns consumers of
  potential financial scams during the holiday season\nDec 1\, 2021\nGARDIN
 ER – As the holiday season approaches\, Maine’s Bureau of Financial
  Institutions Superintendent Lloyd LaFountain is reminding consumers to b
 e on the lookout for potential scams targeting consumers’ financial inf
 ormation\, including their debit and credit cards:\n“The holidays are an
  active time of year for scammers seeking to target unsuspecting consumers
  and illegally gain access to their finances. Consumers should remain vigi
 lant throughout the season’s festivities to ensure their money is well 
 protected and securethrough the holiday season.”\nWhile scams can target
  consumers at any time\, Superintendent LaFountain notes that scammer acti
 vity may increase during the holiday season\, when peoples’ busy schedu
 les and holiday shopping leaves them with less time to watch their financ
 es. Consumers should continue to monitor their bank accounts and report an
 y unauthorized charges to their financial institutions. Also\, holiday sho
 ppers should beware of gift card scams\, and know that a reputable financi
 al institution\, government agency\, or utility company will never ask you
  to pay an outstanding bill or charge using a gift card.\n“Best practice
 s for using debit and credit cards throughout the year should be followed 
 during the holidays as well. Consumers are reminded to never provide their
  PIN numbers\, online banking passwords\, and personal information to anot
 her person or company that appears untrustworthy. Credit unions and banks 
 will never text\, call\, or email a consumer requesting this information. 
 Do not reply to unsolicited emails. A good rule of thumb is to contact you
 r bank or credit union directly if you receive a suspicious message.\nMany
  consumers see the holiday season as the perfect time to give to their fav
 orite charities. Superintendent LaFountain urges consumers to be wary of f
 ake charities targeting their goodwill. Consumers looking\nhttps://www.mai
 ne.gov/pfr/financialinstitutions/news-notices/2022-05-16-maine-financial-i
 nstitutions-superintendent-warns-consumers-potential
URL:https://www.maine.gov/pfr/financialinstitutions/news-notices/2022-05-1
 6-maine-financial-institutions-superintendent-warns-consumers-potential
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20b5d189e626f655@role-consumer-protection.maine-government-feeds
