DTSTAMP:20260802T111854Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Termination of Agency Relationships and Maine
 ’s Cancellation Control Acts
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE  \nDEPA RTMENT O F P R OFES SIO NAL  & FINA NCI
 AL  RE GUL ATIO N  \nBUREAU OF INSU RAN CE  \n \n \n \n \n \nOffice Locati
 on: 76 Northern Avenue\, Gardiner\, Maine 04345 \nMailing Address: 34 Stat
 e House Station\, Augusta\, Maine 04333 \nwww.maine.gov/pfr/insurance \nPh
 one: (207) 624-8475 TTY: Please Call Maine Relay 711 Consumer Assistance: 
 1-800-300-5000 Fax: (207) 624-8599 \n \nJanet T. Mills \nGovernor \nRobert
  L. Carey \nSuperintendent \n \nJoan F. Cohen \nCommissioner \n \n Bulleti
 n 489 \nTermination of Agency Relationships and Maine’s Cancellation Con
 trol Acts \nIt has come to the Bureau’s attention that some Maine consum
 ers have recently had their homeowners\, renters\, \nor personal auto poli
 cies nonrenewed solely because the insurer’s agency relationship with a 
 producer has \nterminated. This is not a lawful basis for nonrenewal. \n \
 nInsurers are reminded that in Maine\, these lines of business are subject
  to Cancellation Control Acts that grant \npolicyholders the right to rene
 w their policies unless the insurer can demonstrate a valid reason for non
 renewal. \nThe only permissible reasons for nonrenewal are those specified
  in the Maine Automobile Insurance \nCancellation Control Act1 or the Main
 e Property Cancellation Control Act\,2 as applicable. For all policies tha
 t \nare subject to either Control Act\, the reason or reasons for nonrenew
 al action must be explicitly stated in the \nnotice of nonrenewal. Vague e
 xplanations such as “underwriting reasons” are insufficient.3  \n \nPr
 oducers who no longer represent a particular insurer are free to offer pol
 icyholders alternative coverage with a \ndifferent insurer\, but that does
  not extinguish the policyholders’ right to renew the coverage they have
 . The \nrights of policyholders and the obligations of insurers and produc
 ers in these situations are discussed in detail in \nBulletin 391\, Person
 al Lines Agency Terminations and Book Rollovers\, which insurers and produ
 cers are \nencouraged to review prior to the termination of an agency rela
 ti\nhttps://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/file
 s/inline-files/489.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/file
 s/inline-files/489.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
